    <node id="Paper_2287">
      <data key="d0">Paper</data>
      <data key="d1">Vis</data>
      <data key="d2">2022</data>
      <data key="d3">Supporting Expressive and Faithful Pictorial Visualization Design with Visual Style Transfer</data>
      <data key="d4">10.1109/tvcg.2022.3209486</data>
      <data key="d5">http://dx.doi.org/10.1109/TVCG.2022.3209486</data>
      <data key="d6">236.0</data>
      <data key="d7">246.0</data>
      <data key="d8">J</data>
      <data key="d9">Pictorial visualizations portray data with figurative messages and approximate the audience to the visualization. Previous research on pictorial visualizations has developed authoring tools or generation systems, but their methods are restricted to specific visualization types and templates. Instead, we propose to augment pictorial visualization authoring with visual style transfer, enabling a more extensible approach to visualization design. To explore this, our work presents Vistylist, a design support tool that disentangles the visual style of a source pictorial visualization from its content and transfers the visual style to one or more intended pictorial visualizations. We evaluated Vistylist through a survey of example pictorial visualizations, a controlled user study, and a series of expert interviews. The results of our evaluation indicated that Vistylist is useful for creating expressive and faithful pictorial visualizations.</data>
      <data key="d10">Yang Shi 0007;Pei Liu;Siji Chen;Mengdi Sun;Nan Cao 0001</data>
      <data key="d11">Yang Shi;Pei Liu;Siji Chen;Mengdi Sun;Nan Cao</data>
      <data key="d12">Intelligent Big Data Visualization Lab, Tongji University, China;Intelligent Big Data Visualization Lab, Tongji University, China;Intelligent Big Data Visualization Lab, Tongji University, China;Intelligent Big Data Visualization Lab, Tongji University, China;Intelligent Big Data Visualization Lab, Tongji University, China</data>
      <data key="d13">10.1109/tvcg.2016.2598647;10.1109/tvcg.2013.234;10.1109/tvcg.2019.2934810;10.1109/tvcg.2019.2934785;10.1109/tvcg.2016.2598620;10.1109/tvcg.2021.3114775;10.1109/tvcg.2020.3030406;10.1109/tvcg.2020.3030448;10.1109/tvcg.2010.179;10.1109/tvcg.2020.3030403;10.1109/tvcg.2016.2598647</data>
      <data key="d14">Pictorial visualization,data-driven design</data>
      <data key="d15" />
      <data key="d16">10.0</data>
      <data key="d17">80.0</data>
      <data key="d18">1612.0</data>
      <data key="d19">HM</data>
      <data key="d20" />
    </node>
